+      "logical_name": "sharp-binomial-block-symmetric-tensor-recovery-draft",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Sharp block-symmetric tensor recovery, review pending",
+      "statement": "Prover-written mathematical claim; independent review pending. Let H,W be finite-dimensional real Hilbert spaces, 1<=p<=q, and T in H^(tensor(p+q)) tensor W. Assume T is symmetric in its first p positions and separately its next q positions. If P_q averages permutations of the first q positions, leaving all others fixed, then ||T||<=binom(q,p)||P_qT|| in the Hilbert tensor norm. The factor is optimal when dim H>=2 and W is nonzero. The case p=d,q=2d has factor binom(2d,d); BKL Lemma 2.2 already obtains this factor in its proof before stating the coarser 4^d bound. Complete incidence-identity and explicit sharpness proofs are in w348/ATTEMPT.md L1; this is not a full KLS proof.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
