+      "title": "KLS route: universal all-degree tilt input remains unaudited here",
+      "statement": "Unproved input in the w348 packet. The full analytic statement sought is one universal R>=1 such that every centered full-dimensional log-concave probability mu with Cov(mu)<=I, every f in L2(mu), and every d>=1 satisfy ||T_df||_HS<=R^d||f||_2 for the normalized ordered tilt Taylor tensor. On the regular subclass used by BKL, Theorem 3.1 of arXiv:2610.05474v1 states that this input implies C_P(mu)<=C R^2 with a numerical C. That reduction, its general-measure approximation, and the Cheeger comparison are externally supplied steps here. The general all-degree input is not established or independently audited by this packet; published authors claim to establish it through cumulants and suspension.",
