+      "title": "Exact all-degree tilt norm for centered exponential products",
+      "statement": "Prover-written mathematical claim; independent review pending. Let Y_1,...,Y_n be independent Exp(1) variables, X_i=Y_i-1, and mu the law of X. For every n>=1 and d>=1, the operator f -> T_df=(1/d!)D^dF_f(0), from L2(mu) to the ordered-index Hilbert--Schmidt tensor space, has norm exactly sqrt(binom(2d-2,d-1)). Thus ||T_df||<=2^(d-1)||f||_2 and R=2 is the smallest base valid in ||T_df||<=R^d||f||_2 for all degrees in this family. Equality is attained by the normalized one-coordinate polynomial P_d(Y_1), where P_d(y)=y^d/d!-y^(d-1)/(d-1)!. The proof separates orthogonal coordinate supports before bounding each positive frame-operator trace. The law is isotropic and log-concave but nonsmooth, so this direct calculation does not invoke the regularity-dependent BKL criterion. It does not supply the input for arbitrary log-concave laws.",
